messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cofflink.c
Line: 3165
Function: coff_relocate_section
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: In the bfd_reloc_overflow case, the code unconditionally dereferences sym (sym->n_sclass and passes sym to bfd_coff_classify_symbol) without checking that sym is non-NULL. Elsewhere in this function sym is treated as potentially NULL (e.g., at line 3114). If the relocation overflows on a relocation that references an external symbol (where sym can be NULL), this path will dereference a NULL pointer.

Source context:
